line session with them which I'll put  a link to below called rather  ambitiously introduction to reading  Hegel and so we did a online hangout  with with them I had to cancel the  worlds of speculative fiction lecture  again because of the the injury and all  the other things that kind of piled up  so we cancelled that and put it off  until August I did manage to hold you  know a few online events the the AMA we  did philosophy pop-ups of course  oriented towards the issue of the body  understood in a philosophical  perspective and I held my two half-hour  Hagel Q&amp;A and discussion sessions I also  attended the Marquette Aristotle and the  Aristotelian tradition conference and  got to hang out with you know some old  friends and colleagues and also you know  the trumble's who came down from Toronto  some some people that I've been involved  with for quite a while mostly in an  online manner but we met at we met up at  stoical on last year which is very nice  and they're a great couple so we got to  chat a bit and and go to the picnic and  then of course we had our MKE stoic  fellowship meeting at the end of the  month we started doing Epictetus  discourse isn't we had a few new people  show up that's always kind of nice to  see I did remain quite busy with  tutorial sessions I actually picked up  some new clients doing consulting work  and doing philosophical counseling I've  also been quite busy developing syllabi  for the classes that I'll be teaching in  the fall for Marquette  and the Milwaukee Institute of Art and  Design I tried to get some writing done  and I did get some work done in Iraq sis  D&amp;O @tk but I didn't get any of the  guest blogging that I wanted to do  accomplished or much in the heavy metal  philosopher or half hour Hagel blog but  I'm hoping to get to that this coming  month video wise I finished up the core  concept videos on Heidegger and started  releasing some of the videos that I had  previously only released to my patreon  supporters on Plato's Republic book 10 I  did five of the half hour Hagel videos I  usually actually get six done a month  but I only managed to get five done and  I released a few Q&amp;A videos and of  course there were videos of the online  events I did however manage to get and  my son helped me out with some of the  editing on a few of these some podcast  episodes in the Sadler's samplers  lectures out on Plato on the apology the  credo and the Euthyphro so all told you  know a pretty busy month I didn't get as  much accomplished as I would like but  it's quite understandable given the  circumstances alright let's talk about  the month of July now so we have a few  face-to-face events and some online  events coming up on July 10th at 5:00  p.m. this is an online event we'll be  having our public half-hour Haegele Q&amp;A  session under written of course by my  half hour Haegele patreon supporters on  the 12th here locally at the Brookfield  Public Library we're gonna have I think  this is probably going to be a kind of a  big draw we're going to be talking about  Robert Howard and the Conan stories that  that he wrote and some of the history of  other people editing those that's part  of the worlds of speculative fiction  series 7:00 p.m. at the Brookfield  Public Library so if you're here in the  area and want to  about classic swords and sorcery and  some of the philosophical themes show up  to that on the 14th at 12 p.m. noon  central time of course I'll be having my  monthly AMA that is ask me anything  session so you can pop in and ask  whatever questions you like and if you  get them in early enough I will  certainly make an effort to answer them  if you wait until the very end we  usually have so many questions that I  can't get to all of them  then on the 26th at 6:00 p.m. here in  Milwaukee at the Shorewood Public  Library we'll be having our MKE stoic  fellowship monthly meeting again going  through Epictetus the second part of  book 1 of the discourses and then on the  28th at the Milwaukee Public Library  central branch 11:30 a.m. we will be  having our  MKE Sophia that society of philosophers  in America chapter membership meeting so  this is for members of course anybody  can become a member if you if you want  to and Sophia is a organization spread  throughout the United States that's  devoted to doing public philosophy that  is bringing philosophy to bear on public  problems and in public ways in in  fostering civil discourse and that's  what we're going to be discussing so a  lot of events happening I will also be  doing my philosophy pop ups I announce  those on patreon at the beginning of the  month and I'll be handling that later  today everybody else finds out the day  of one is in YouTube live one is in  Facebook live and this month I'm going  to talk about the family as a you know  philosophical construct as well as you  know all the other things that it is and  I think that could be quite interesting  for people very busy month ahead in  terms of tutorial sessions more  consulting work with two different  projects philosophical counseling I'm  also still continuing developing the  syllabus  I've got that more or less worked out  from my philosophy of human nature  course my philosophical foundations  course now it's time for me to start  hammering away at the business ethics  course that I'm gonna be teaching for  Marquette in the fall and on revising my  my syllabus and course structure for the  world views and values class that I  teach from Marist also in the fall  online and I'm trying to get more  writing done this month we'll see how  that goes both popular writing and  academic writing and some work on the  the book project doing a lot of  editorial work of course your stoicism  today and I'm also lining up speaking  gigs both for the fall and for first  quarter and second quarter of 2019 so if  you're interested in bringing me in as a  speaker I'm already pretty booked up for  the fall but 2019 i